    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;Collapse Of The Midnight Sun&quot;</strong> is a cozy indie game with metroidvania and time loop mechanics that is less than one hour long and developed from scratch by a single developer. You'll be exploring an island that used to be a mountain before the city next to it flooded. The human made fusion reaction that lights up the sky as if it was the <i>sun</i>, has started to collapse. You only have a couple of minutes before it does and time resets. During these couple of minutes, you'll explore  the island and\u00a0memorize its locations like\u00a0<i>the abandoned</i> <i>train station</i> and tools like\u00a0<i>the lantern.</i> Memorizing these will be crucial for solving the puzzles ahead, before the next collapse and the resulting time loop.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;Collapse Of The Midnight Sun&quot;</strong> is a cozy indie game with metroidvania and time loop mechanics that is less than one hour long and developed from scratch by a single developer. You'll be exploring an island that used to be a mountain before the city next to it flooded. The human made fusion reaction that lights up the sky as if it was the <i>sun</i>, has started to collapse. You only have a couple of minutes before it does and time resets. During these couple of minutes, you'll explore  the island and\u00a0memorize its locations like\u00a0<i>the abandoned</i> <i>train station</i> and tools like\u00a0<i>the lantern.</i> Memorizing these will be crucial for solving the puzzles ahead, before the next collapse and the resulting time loop.</p>",
